+## D9 — Add a promotion-only parametric family without changing production
+
+The native adapter in `workspace/parametric/adapter.py` exposes one strict parameter,
+`target_scope`, with values `all_horizontal` and `nearest_vertical`. The default
+materializes the exact canonical Racket source (SHA-256
+`bba257d19e2b9ed977892b09ef1fa837029e8c9a96a819e0d356d2c04f708f44`); the composed
+setting materializes SHA-256
+`4fe45e1b31173ea2411c73ffe9a7f11e306d2ef585d19b92cb0ef1efd9aa73a3`.
+The production generator remains byte-identical at SHA-256
+`b63464a0ca49196e4166345f842ace658b6e90ae32e31488d77fd9ae5ae5cb16`.
+Inputs are setting-neutral and deterministically scheduled by role/index, so demo and
+query prefixes remain stable while counts vary independently over demos 2..6 and queries
+1..8.
+
+## D10 — Make the composed setting depend on an input-specific intermediate
+
+Step A locates the unique vertical gray domino. Its absolute cell coordinates are the
+intermediate. Step B chooses the unique horizontal gray domino with minimum Manhattan
+cell distance to that intermediate and recolors it cyan. This is not a fixed position
+shortcut: protected Racket replay of a `skip_a` top-left ablation changes the final output
+on every retained witness case. The source-bound witness is
+`checks/e46c2557ad08/sequential-dependency.json`; its protected replay receipt is
+`checks/e46c2557ad08/sequential-replay.json`.
+
+## D11 — Reveal queries one at a time without a total-count hint
+
+`prototype.public_turn` projects exactly one query input plus the demonstrations. It emits
+no query index, total count, future query, query output, program, setting, seed or private
+receipt. The first visible turn is byte-identical for episodes with the same demos and
+first query whether the controller stores one query or eight. Eight saved canonical public
+turns passed `check_public_exports.py`; evidence is
+`checks/e46c2557ad08/public-export-check.json`.
+
+## D12 — Retain native qualification, boundary evidence and the owner handoff
+
+The current source/evidence inventory is
+`workspace/parametric/evidence/manifest.json` (SHA-256
+`9a495e0bd07888dfcff72e939bbd9f7c298339866e79ab201796c1d7b0264c39`). Protected native
+qualification is `checks/e46c2557ad08/qualification/qualification.json` (SHA-256
+`bfef6dd2a8108cabc0bac91f26e0982429939b57e589324069fa041e8c9256ba`) with 40 protected
+Racket evaluations across both settings and seeds 0 and 17. The bounded edge sweep covered
+320 episodes, 2,720 pairs, seeds 0, 1, 17 and `2**63-1`, every supported count, and the
+30×30/16-target profile with no artifact findings; see
+`checks/e46c2557ad08/edge-sweep.json`. One initial sweep failure is retained separately:
+it compared first turns against a six-demo episode and therefore tested the checker rather
+than hidden-query invariance; the corrected comparison holds demo count fixed.
+
+This work is reviewer-reported `ready`, not owner-accepted and not training-admitted. The
+next useful action is owner integration followed by fresh native qualification and
+acceptance replay against the integrated source inventory. Optional peer targets
+`bca4f37ec5e9` and `deb48f07adde` were left unchanged because MAIN completion and evidence
+took priority.
